          "issue": "I haven't started the quick workflow yet, because the toast wording is yours to choose and nothing can be written until you pick. Once you choose, I'll run the planner, plan-checker, executor and verifier. The wording goes into `copyFallback(address)` in `src/lib/copy.ts`, and the test `copyFallback names the address` goes into `tests/unit/copy.test.ts`. `COPY_FALLBACK` stays exported and unchanged.\n\nOption 2 says the mail app will open. `src/components/ui/useCopyEmail.ts` is in your allowed paths, but nothing in this item changes its behavior. If the hook doesn't open the mail app on failure, that sentence would be wrong, so keep that in mind when choosing.\n\nWhich toast wording should `copyFallback` return when copying the email fails?\n1. `Couldn’t copy. Email me at <address>.`\n2. `Couldn’t copy the address. Opening your mail app to <address>.`",
          "recommendation": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "key": "1",
              "kind": "choice",
              "label": "`Couldn’t copy. Email me at <address>.`"
            },
